## Day to day

Things that are easy to miss and worth knowing early.

**Adding a task moves you into it.** MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec add parser MACRO_INLINE_CODE creates the task and puts
your shell in its directory, ready to work. Pass MACRO_INLINE_CODE -N MACRO_INLINE_CODE to create it and stay
where you are.

**Almost nothing needs arguments.** MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec cat MACRO_INLINE_CODE , MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec set -P high MACRO_INLINE_CODE and
MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec rm MACRO_INLINE_CODE act on the current task. Name a task only when you mean a
different one.

**MACRO_INLINE_CODE - MACRO_INLINE_CODE means "the previous one" at every level.** MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec cd - MACRO_INLINE_CODE for tasks,
MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec env cd - MACRO_INLINE_CODE for environments, and the same for desks. Forgotten which is
which? MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec ls -t MACRO_INLINE_CODE prints just the current and previous task.

**Deleting what you are standing in is safe.** Remove the task you are inside and
Tec moves your shell to the previous task first, or to the desk if that was the
last one. The session is never left in a directory deleted underneath it.

**Tasks carry a little metadata.** A type — MACRO_INLINE_CODE task MACRO_INLINE_CODE , MACRO_INLINE_CODE bugfix MACRO_INLINE_CODE ,
MACRO_INLINE_CODE feature MACRO_INLINE_CODE , MACRO_INLINE_CODE hotfix MACRO_INLINE_CODE — and a priority from MACRO_INLINE_CODE lowest MACRO_INLINE_CODE to
MACRO_INLINE_CODE highest MACRO_INLINE_CODE , set with MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec set -T bugfix -P high MACRO_INLINE_CODE . Anything else you
want to record is a file in the task directory.

**Names are short on purpose.** A task ID is up to 8 characters, environment and
desk names up to 10. Skip the ID entirely and Tec generates one: 00000001, 00000002
and so on. MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec mv MACRO_INLINE_CODE renames a task you later think better of.

**Aliases save keystrokes.** MACRO_INLINE_CODE dir = "ls" MACRO_INLINE_CODE in the config makes MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec dir MACRO_INLINE_CODE
run MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec ls MACRO_INLINE_CODE ; MACRO_INLINE_CODE els = "env ls" MACRO_INLINE_CODE works for subcommands too.

**When something misbehaves**, colors, hooks and debug output can each be flipped
for a single run with MACRO_INLINE_CODE -C MACRO_INLINE_CODE , MACRO_INLINE_CODE -H MACRO_INLINE_CODE and MACRO_INLINE_CODE -D MACRO_INLINE_CODE , as in
MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec -H off ls MACRO_INLINE_CODE . And MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec help COMMAND MACRO_INLINE_CODE explains any command in
full.

